Grmbl2 wasn't stupid. People always said he was, but he wasn't. He just 
didn't know how to read. He also didn't waste any time with religion, 
which he found useless. His way was to bash things, since this always 
made his problem go away. So he started his journey in search of the 
amulet. Just to show'em.

He started as usual, with his pet dog Slasher. Before he went, his tribe 
leader told him about puzzle rooms he had to pass, and described how to 
solve them. He was afraid he'd forget, so he went there as soon as 
possible. He tamed a cat there, and named it Gnasher. At the top, he 
found a bag which made his stuff much lighter. Good, Grmbl2 thought; 
that'll give me more strength to bash things.

He then went into the mines, where his fellow dwarves lived. There, he 
met a distant relative. It had tentacles on its head, and tried to suck 
his brains out. He didn't have much to begin with, so he kept his 
distance, and killed it with a wand of cold. He also found a weird 
marker, but he didn't know how to write.

Mine town had a bookshop, among others. But he couldn't enter, since he 
had made himself invisible to escape from that tentacle-thing. It seemed 
like a good idea at the time. He looked all around, and finally found 
some bandages, which he wrapped around himself. Now the shopkeepers 
could see him, and they let him in. In the shops, he found a whistle 
that made his pets appear instantly, and some expensive water that his 
pets liked to pick up.

He went further down in the mines. At the end, he found rooms and mazes, 
with even more books in them. He just left them there: maybe someone 
else could use them. He did find some nice boots, a nice cloak, and an 
interesting gray stone, so this trip wasn't all bad [his AC was now 
-10]. He tried to find more good gear, but found only really bad stuff, 
and it wouldn't come off. He met a weird, sex-crazed creature that could 
take them off once, and getting them wet in fountains worked as well.

Burning and rusting were becoming major problems for him. He'd find some 
nice clothes, and a centaur would come up to him and shoot fire, burning 
his cloak. Then a rust monster would touch his shoes, and they'd go bad 
as well. To get back at them, he just bashed and poked with his spear.

As he got deep in the dungeon, he found a very creepy room. There were 
lots of scary monsters there, and lots of items. The items were drawing 
him in, but in the end, the scary monsters won, and he fled upstairs 
again. [a bones file with a barbed devil, jabberwock, minotaur, and a 
ki-rin that was peaceful]

In the mean time he had some new pets (his old pets had died). He had 
called them Slasher5 and Gnasher3. He then found a place where he could 
turn them from dog and cat into other creatures. They became a baby 
yellow dragon and a vampire lord. With these powerful creatures, he felt 
safe enough to enter a big castle he'd found. Gnasher3 murdered all the 
soldiers there.

All the stuff the soldiers had was sorted and the useful stuff was 
picked out. the rest was put in piles, and with a wand he found, he 
changed it into other stuff. He created a helm that made his little 
pea-mind bounce around in his head, boots that made his feet go very 
fast, and a cloak that everything slipped off. He only wore the helmet, 
since the rest didn't protect him enough. [some water accident had 
dropped his AC to -8, -5 with speed boots]

He saved some spears from that big castle, and brought them to a 
shopkeeper. The shopkeeper looked very interested in one of them, so he 
kept it as his main weapon [a +5 spear!]. Now, he felt strong enough to 
take on those nasty monsters deep in the dungeon.

A great fiery demon was there. He zapped it with a wand, and it fell to 
sleep. Grmbl2 bashed it to death, and had one less problem. A horned 
creature, half man half bull, was killed together with Gnasher3, the 
vampire lord. He was then warned that there was another creature there, 
but he couldn't see what it was. Well, he didn't mind, so he started 
bashing it. It hit back hard! It took his best healing potions, and two 
lesser ones, to stay alive, but he finished it off. Now he had a chance 
to check out his loot.

And some loot it was. He recognized several legendary weapons. There 
were several special capes, boots and gloves. There were scales of 
dragons, and lots of magic wands, rings and potions. He ignored the 
spellbooks, scrolls and markers. He crossed some x's into the dust with 
the wands, and a voice asked him what he wished. He asked for a 
protective armor, like that of a magical dragon, and he got it [+3 gray 
dragon scale mail].

Now he looked better, and found that this level was a grave to two other 
adventurers. One of them had been a thief, he figured, and the other 
wizard. He found another armor like his, only it looked silver, not 
gray. There was also a magical key. He also found really good boots, a 
superb shirt, and a helmet that his pet vampire lord sadly got to first 
[+5 gauntlets of dexterity, +5 hawaiian t-shirt, a +4 or +5 helm of 
brilliance, and +5 silver dragon scale mail]. He wore the shirt and the 
gloves, but kept his own armor, and enhanced it with a shiny shield.

Grmbl2 went on, bashing some weird woman with snakes on her head, and 
descending further. Suddenly, his loyal vampire lord disappeared. He 
went looking for it, and found it, still tame, 10 stairs up. In the mean 
time, he also tamed two very big worms with enormous appetites. He took 
these, and his vampire lord, further down, and together they cleaned out 
another castle.

He went back up to sort through all his stuff, when he suddenly found 
himself back home! They needed help, but said he'd first have to take 
off his helmet; he did, thinking to himself he'd put it back on later. 
Turned out there was a dragon killing everyone. Well, no problem a 
little bashing can't cure!

He went down, found the foul beast's lair, and killed it with ease. He 
took the big mace and the bell it had stolen, and went back up. When he 
wanted to give them back, the leader said he should keep them. If they 
didn't want the things, why did he have to go get them? He left his home 
caves, and put his helmet back on.

He now did some last preparations before heading further down. He took 
his new stuff to a shopkeeper, to ask what he thought of it. Afterward, 
one of the worms ate him! He then did some mixing of different potions, 
they way his leader told him. In the end, he had 42 superb healing 
potions [raised his hp from 152 to 392, keeping 10].

Just before entering what he'd later find out to be hell, he became 
resistant to fire (finally), although his equipment still wasn't [AC was 
now -20, and would be for the rest of the game]. One of his worms died, 
the other turned into an acidic blob, but his vampire lord stayed by his 
side. Together they descended further and further... At what he thought 
must be the bottom (since there were no stairs further down) he found a 
spot where the ground shook. He marked it, and went back up.

On his way up, he found a tower, with a wimpy vampire at the top. He 
killed it, and took its candlestick. Maybe he could kill things with it? 
Then he tried to look in a chest there, and it exploded, together with 
the wand that gave him his wish, another wand that killed things 
instantly, and a ring that increased the damage his spear did [by 4]. 
Back in hell, his spear rusted further, after already being rusty from 
one of those hellish rust monsters.

He now remembered he had some candles back up in his chest, so he went 
to get them. Stupid of him not to bring those along in the first place. 
He then went back to hell, to explore another tower he'd found. Here, he 
found a wizard. He didn't like wizards; they always taunted him, since 
he couldn't read. So he bashed him, and he died. He took the book the 
wizard was carrying, since it seemed special.

Now where was he to go? He went to the shaking spot, but couldn't find 
anything there. He lit his candles, so he could see better. Nothing. He 
dropped his bell, and it made a terrifying noise. Maybe there was 
something in that weird book? He opened it, and at the same time, the 
earth opened up in front of him. A way further down!

The wizard had apparently not died, and met him there. He had another 
wand that instantly killed, and used it. He then put on a ring that made 
all the monsters fight among themselves, and went into the central room, 
where he killed annoying guy in the robe, because he had the amulet. He 
wanted to get out, and that was the only way, he'd been told. [he broke 
atheist conduct here, sadly. His knapsack couldn't accommodate more 
items when he wanted to pick up the amulet, so he dropped something. On 
the altar. DAMN!]

On the way back up, he was pulled back 5 times when climbing the stairs, 
but never far. That wizard guy wouldn't die, and they had a big fight 
around the house of that snake woman. He took all his valuables from his 
chest, and killed that wizard again; finally, he'd arrived at the top. 
And just as he thought he'd arrive home, there was that wizard again, in 
a world made of only earth! What was this? Oh well, only one thing to 
do: bash.

The wizard called in two wizards that looked like they were already 
dead, and they called in even more creatures. Grmbl2 almost died, but 
luckily, he had those great healing potions. He used a crystal ball to 
find out where to go next. It showed a place with nothing but clouds; he 
went there, and the ball showed nothing. Suddenly, a creature there 
disappeared. He followed it with his vampire lord.

Now there was fire everywhere, and lava. He hated fire. He got caught in 
a fire vortex, and when he bashed his way out, he was embedded in lava! 
He quickly used one of his magic wands to kill the lava, and dug himself 
out. His boots hadn't survived, but even though that slowed him down, he 
wanted to get out. But his crystal ball still showed nothing, so he 
wandered around. He felt sad when Gnasher3, his loyal buddy, died. But 
finally he found a way out, and entered a world of only water. He put on 
his slippery cloak, and quickly found a way out.

He now arrived in a place with lots of white, winged creatures. It 
seemed they didn't approve of his ring that caused fighting, but he 
didn't care. He just wanted out. He went to the right side, using a 
corpse of a chicken-like creature to wade through the hordes of hostile 
beings. But he couldn't get out there. So he went back, and tried the 
left side. No way out either. His head ached in here. He took of his 
helmet. "I just want out!" he cried. "I don't want the stupid amulet! I 
just want out! Whoever gets me out, can have it!". And so it happened...

Grmbl2, lawful male dwarven Caveman //he'd been chaotic since Ludios, 
apart from the quest and the final moment.

