** Some random thoughts **

All in all, a nice game. It was a shame about the atheism mistake. 
Atheist isn't really that hard a challenge. Good pet use can show you 
what's cursed, holy and unholy water can be found, and protection isn't 
really needed, and neither are artifacts. Combined with illiterate it 
was harder, and the bones file helped a lot. The master key of thievery 
effectively doubled my HP, and the enchanted items couldn't have been 
acquired any other way. If I hadn't found it, I would have used more 
wishes. I wanted to wish for one or two quest artifacts (hadn't found 
any artifacts before the bones) once I reached the castle.
Spears aren't the best throwing weapons: they're too heavy and you can 
only throw one each turn. Dagger would have been worse for a caveman 
though, I think.
I think I'll try another atheist illiterate, to get a _real_ atheist, 
and to see if I can do it without a good bones file. Or maybe I'll try a 
pacifist first; I liked having lots of pets.

Erik


